course: dictionary
lesson: 14390
title: Oscillating: swinging back and forth
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Oscillating means moving or swinging back and forth again and again, in a steady way. Think of a playground swing going forwards, then backwards, then forwards. «The pendulum on the old clock was oscillating, tick after tick.» The clue is «tick after tick»: the swinging keeps going on and on, so oscillating means swinging back and forth regularly.
explain: The word can describe a thing that turns from side to side. «The fan on the desk is oscillating, so the cool air reaches the whole room.» The fan is not spinning in one circle; it turns one way, then the other, then back again. You can check by swapping in your meaning: "the fan is swinging back and forth" still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes oscillating is about feelings or states, not objects. «Her mood kept oscillating between excitement and worry before the test.» She was not stuck in one feeling. She kept moving from excited to worried and back again. Ask yourself: is something going back and forth between two things? If yes, oscillating might fit.
fact: Oscillating means swinging or moving back and forth regularly.
fact: The verb is oscillate, and its forms are oscillates, oscillated and oscillating.
fact: «Oscillating» can describe a thing that turns from side to side, like a fan.
fact: Scientists use oscillating to describe pendulums, waves and springs that swing back and forth.
fact: When you see oscillating, look for clues like «back and forth», «from side to side» or «again and again».
exercise: «The fan on the desk is oscillating, turning from side to side.» What does oscillating mean? | *Moving back and forth | Standing perfectly still | Falling quickly to the floor | Making a loud noise
exercise: «The pendulum on the clock was oscillating, tick after tick.» Which words in the sentence give you a clue to the meaning? | *Tick after tick | Oscillating and clock | Clock and pendulum | Was and the
exercise: «Her mood kept oscillating between excitement and worry.» What does this tell you about her mood? | It stayed the same all day | It hid completely | *It changed back and forth between two feelings | It grew bigger and bigger without stopping
test: «The garden sprinkler was oscillating, spraying water from left to right.» What is the sprinkler doing? | *Swinging from side to side | Sinking into the grass | Turning off | Dripping in one spot
test: Ruby says oscillating means "shining brightly". Why is she wrong? | Because it is a noun, not a verb | Because shining is a colour | Because she is correct, it means shining | *Because oscillating means swinging back and forth, not giving out light
exam: «The bridge swayed as the wind kept oscillating through the valley.» What does oscillating mean in this sentence? | Breaking into pieces | *Swinging back and forth | Growing taller | Sleeping
